{
  "id": "jol",
  "term": "JOL",
  "definition": "JOL stands for judgment of learning, a person’s prediction of how likely they are to remember something later after studying it. It is used in self-regulated learning and reflects subjective metamemory, which can be fairly accurate overall but may differ from actual later memory performance, especially when judged immediately after learning.",
